// Fixed objects: each is placed exactly once per world, whatever the terrain there, and random
// objects (rocks, pebbles) stay off its footprint and `clearance` tiles around it.
//
// A placement is (object, at, [offset], [clearance]):
//   object:    an object kind from objects.ron
//   at:        Spawn            the tile the game centres its map on, where players spawn
//              Pole(inset: n)   n tiles in from the north or the south edge, on the spawn's
//                               meridian; the seed picks the pole (the south edge, largest y,
//                               for an even number of set seed bits), like the expedition's
//                               polar site
//   offset:    (x, y) tiles from the site to the footprint's centre; +y is drawn up on screen
//   clearance: tiles around the footprint kept free of random objects
// The footprint is pushed back inside the world if it would reach past an edge. Keep fixed
// objects apart: they do not avoid each other.
(
    placements: [
        // The crashed ship, its south edge 2 tiles above the players' spawn.
        (object: "ship_hull", at: Spawn, offset: (0, 11), clearance: 3),
        // Its engine broke off over a pole, at the expedition's polar site (512 world units,
        // 16 tiles, in from the edge).
        (object: "ship_engine", at: Pole(inset: 16), clearance: 2),
        // Ship parts are not placed here: they spawn in sulfur basins (objects.ron
        // `ship_wreckage`).
    ],
)
